  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Aikatuk</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AIKATUK is the Indigenous association of the Kaxuyana, Tunayana, and Kahyana peoples in southern Karib, Par&#xe1;. After helping establish both the organization and their 19,000 km&#xb2; territory - now home to 19 villages and about 550 people - Regnskogsf&#xf6;reningen is providing direct support. The project strengthens youth-led communication for territorial protection, trains Indigenous communicators and environmental agents, and has established a new defense base and river patrol system to combat invasions and safeguard the Wayamu territory.</narrative>
  </description>
